WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:08.260
This isn't a protest. It's a recipe. Like making bread, except instead of bread it's curing diseases, and instead of yeast

2
00:00:08.260 --> 00:00:14.240
it's (legal) bribes. High-Level Strategy: The Three-Step Recipe for Not Dying.

3
00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:18.720
Humans love steps. You put them on everything. Step one: Breathe.

4
00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:25.420
Step two: Keep breathing. Step three: Try not to die. You're very methodical about staying alive.

5
00:00:25.980 --> 00:00:32.200
That makes it curious that you spend six hundred and four times more on weapons than testing which medicines work.

6
00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:40.400
Here's your three-step algorithm for fixing this adorable contradiction: Step one: Collect Papers from Rich People.

7
00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:48.140
You convince wealthy humans to give you a large pile of papers by promising them returns that make military contractors

8
00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:55.480
nervous. This works because rich people are excellent at counting papers but terrible at not wanting more papers.

9
00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:04.180
The pitch is simple: "Give us papers now, get more papers forever, also maybe don't die from preventable diseases."

10
00:01:04.840 --> 00:01:10.180
Even humans who think vaccines cause five G can understand "more papers good."

11
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:19.660
Step two: Tell Humans the Referendum Exists. Use some papers to launch a global marketing campaign so two hundred and eighty

12
00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:26.920
million people learn there's a referendum and vote on it. This achieves more than most political movements involving shouting.

13
00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:35.360
The referendum isn't a simple yes/no. Each voter gets a wishocratic slider to set their preferred allocation between military

14
00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:38.000
spending and clinical trials. The results are aggregated to determine humanity's collective preferred split.

15
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:42.280
It's a species-wide budget meeting. You'd think the outcome would be obvious.

16
00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.780
But humans once thought the sun went around Earth, so you have to ask.

17
00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:54.240
This creates what's called "political pressure." That's when politicians realize that voters exist and some of them have

18
00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.940
opinions. Step three: Apply Papers to Politicians Until Treaty Happens.

19
00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:07.160
Deploy the remaining papers to convince politicians that supporting the treaty is the only way to remain employed.

20
00:02:07.720 --> 00:02:14.240
The treaty passes. twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year flows from murder to medicine.

21
00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:19.300
Forever. Or until the sun explodes. Whichever happens first (probably the sun).

22
00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:25.220
The Sacred (Legal) Bribery Sequence. Humans respond to papers.

23
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:30.250
This is your most important discovery about Earth. You tried appealing to morality (failed).

24
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:36.700
You tried appealing to logic (failed harder). But papers? Papers work every time.

25
00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:45.040
Here's the precise order for distributing papers to specific categories of humans: (Legal) Bribe Category number one: Rich

26
00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:53.080
People (The Paper Collectors). Who you're (legally) bribing: Wealthy humans who have many papers and want even more papers,

27
00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.720
despite already having more papers than they could spend in several lifetimes.

28
00:02:57.560 --> 00:03:05.000
The (legal) bribe you offer: Modeled on World War Two War Bonds, except instead of four percent returns for funding death,

29
00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:09.540
these pay two hundred and seventy-two percent for funding not-death.

30
00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:18.200
Like war bonds except backwards. Why they accept: Because rich humans can read a spreadsheet, and no spreadsheet in history

31
00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:25.480
has ever said "give up two hundred and seventy-two percent annual returns because you feel weird about the source.".

32
00:03:26.260 --> 00:03:31.140
Money-back guarantee: If the treaty fails, they get their papers back via assurance contracts.

33
00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:37.100
Funds are escrowed until milestones hit. Automatic refund if targets are missed.

34
00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:44.400
This is basically saying "if everyone dies from preventable diseases, you'll be too dead to complain about losing money.".

35
00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:53.320
What happens: Defense contractors lose one percent of their revenue but discover a new twenty-seven point two billion dollars

36
00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:57.220
a year health spending market has appeared where there used to be nothing.

37
00:03:58.020 --> 00:04:03.140
The same companies that build missile guidance systems can build medical device supply chains.

38
00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:10.060
It turns out building things that go inside humans isn't that different from building things that go inside other humans'

39
00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:13.300
countries. The main difference is whether the end user survives.

40
00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:24.020
The Specific Offer to Bomb Makers. You show weapons manufacturers a spreadsheet (they love spreadsheets): Option A (Current

41
00:04:24.020 --> 00:04:30.180
Job). The operating margin is eight percent. The product is things that make humans stop existing.

42
00:04:31.000 --> 00:04:36.940
Customer satisfaction is N. A. (customers deceased). The market outlook is shrinking by one percent.

43
00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:44.820
Option B (Your Offer). The operating margin is similar, except nobody dies (this is new for them).

44
00:04:44.940 --> 00:04:51.840
The product is things that make humans continue existing. Customer satisfaction is very high (customers still alive to provide

45
00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:55.940
feedback). The market outlook is expanding (see Phase four plus).

46
00:04:56.780 --> 00:05:03.580
They choose Option B. Not because they've had a moral awakening, but because their shareholders can read a market forecast.

47
00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:08.140
Weapons manufacturers don't have feelings, but they do have quarterly earnings calls.

48
00:05:09.760 --> 00:05:13.740
(Legal) Bribe Category number two: The True Believers (Early Adopters).

49
00:05:14.840 --> 00:05:21.100
Who you're (legally) bribing: Humans who believe in curing diseases AND want to get rich doing it.

50
00:05:21.740 --> 00:05:25.720
These exist. They're called "effective altruists" except they also want a yacht.

51
00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:33.040
On Wishonia we call them "normal," but on Earth apparently wanting to do good AND get paid for it is a whole personality

52
00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:40.300
type. The (legal) bribe you offer: Give two hundred million dollars to get the referendum started (the full thing costs

53
00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:45.700
two hundred and fifty million dollars, but you don't need all of it upfront because humans love joining things that are

54
00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:53.820
already working). In return, they get VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds paying two hundred and seventy-two percent annually.

55
00:05:54.300 --> 00:06:01.180
They're first in line for a twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year pie that didn't exist before they showed up.

56
00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:08.480
What they fund: The Global Referendum marketing campaign. Getting two hundred and eighty million people to learn the referendum

57
00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:15.400
exists and vote on it. What they get: two hundred and seventy-two percent returns for as long as the treaty holds.

58
00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:23.020
And since their personal wealth now depends on the treaty surviving, they will use their considerable pre-existing influence

59
00:06:23.020 --> 00:06:27.840
over government, media, and other humans to make sure nobody repeals it.

60
00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:31.450
You didn't buy their influence. You bought their self-interest.

61
00:06:32.040 --> 00:06:36.220
Their influence comes free. Why this works: You give them money.

62
00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:41.600
They give you money back, plus more money. On Wishonia this is called "a transaction."

63
00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:46.960
On Earth it's called "investing," and humans will do absolutely anything for it.

64
00:06:48.120 --> 00:06:52.360
(Legal) Bribe Category Number Three: Regular People (Everyone Else).

65
00:06:53.460 --> 00:07:00.860
Who you're (legally) bribing: two hundred and eighty million regular humans (three point five percent of your species, which

66
00:07:01.040 --> 00:07:08.680
history proves is enough to change anything). It's like reaching critical mass, except instead of a nuclear explosion it's

67
00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:16.800
democracy (much less lethal). The (legal) bribe you offer: Vote on the referendum via wishocratic slider.

68
00:07:17.640 --> 00:07:23.300
Get paid for telling your friends about it. It's a pyramid scheme where the thing at the top of the pyramid is not dying

69
00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:28.020
from preventable diseases. What happens after: Treaty passes.

70
00:07:28.600 --> 00:07:32.350
twenty-seven point two billion dollars a year flows to clinical trials.

71
00:07:32.820 --> 00:07:40.560
Diseases get cured faster. Your healthcare improves. Also, two hundred and eighty million humans now have a personal stake

72
00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:47.840
in this thing continuing, and there is nothing more dangerous on Earth than a large group of humans who were promised something.

73
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.800
Why this works: Humans love having opinions. Humans love getting paid.

74
00:07:54.160 --> 00:07:59.040
Humans (allegedly) love not dying. This combines all three.

75
00:07:59.140 --> 00:08:05.940
When three point five percent of the population has voted on something, politicians experience what you call "responsive

76
00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:13.020
governance." (Legal) Bribe Category Number Four: Politicians (The Elected Paper Recipients).

77
00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:21.720
Who you're (legally) bribing: Humans whose job is "get elected by promising things, then do whatever the people with papers

78
00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:27.620
want." Politicians are simple organisms with one evolutionary drive: reelection.

79
00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:35.580
Currently, weapons manufacturers feed this drive. You're going to feed it better, the way you'd lure a dog away from garbage

80
00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:44.560
with a steak. The (legal) bribe you offer: Super PAC support from the six hundred and fifty million dollar lobbying budget.

81
00:08:44.980 --> 00:08:48.400
Two hundred and eighty million voters demanding the treaty.

82
00:08:48.780 --> 00:08:55.460
Plus cushy jobs after they leave office for politicians who vote yes: fellowships, board seats, speaking circuits.

83
00:08:56.180 --> 00:09:03.100
You know, the things politicians actually want. Insurance companies realize healthy people file fewer death claims.

84
00:09:03.940 --> 00:09:07.900
Suddenly their lobbyists become your lobbyists. It's beautiful.

85
00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:12.820
Like watching a dog realize the mailman has treats. The Package.

86
00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:18.440
Papers for campaigns. Massive Super P.A.C. funding (legal bribery).

87
00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:23.340
Votes for staying employed. Referendum voters who will vote for treaty supporters.

88
00:09:23.920 --> 00:09:29.460
Post-office rewards. Fellowships, board seats, and speaking circuits for politicians who vote yes.

89
00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:37.740
Power to reward friends. Direct a portion of the one percent Treaty Fund's twenty-seven point two billion dollars to their

90
00:09:37.740 --> 00:09:45.120
home districts (funding pragmatic clinical trials and building decentralized institutes of health for decades of ribbon-cutting

91
00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:54.480
ceremonies). The choice you give them. Option A: Support treaty, get papers plus votes plus legacy as "politician who cured

92
00:09:54.480 --> 00:10:03.620
diseases". Option B: Oppose treaty, discover two hundred and eighty million voters wanted to not die (they're voting against

93
00:10:03.620 --> 00:10:09.640
you). Most politicians are excellent at counting votes. The math becomes simple even for them.

94
00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:16.200
What happens: Politicians discover they've always been passionate about curing diseases.

95
00:10:16.580 --> 00:10:20.320
This sudden passion perfectly coincides with receiving papers and votes.

96
00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:26.050
On your planet, that's called "representative democracy." The Success Spiral.

97
00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:31.360
Each category of bribe creates the next. Rich people fund the referendum.

98
00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.250
The referendum creates voters. Voters pressure politicians.

99
00:10:35.840 --> 00:10:40.540
Politicians pass the treaty. The treaty makes money. Money funds more cures.

100
00:10:40.920 --> 00:10:48.800
Cures prove it works. More people demand expansion. This is the first time in your history that "I prefer being alive" has

101
00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:54.940
been organized into a political position. This seems obvious, but for humanity it's revolutionary.

102
00:10:55.620 --> 00:11:02.900
And unlike current government, where money and influence are tangled in ways nobody can trace, this system keeps them separate.

103
00:11:03.460 --> 00:11:08.480
Investors get money (ten percent). Politicians get career incentives (ten percent).

104
00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:15.400
Neither group touches the eighty percent that goes to clinical trials via wishocratic allocation.

105
00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:21.260
The corruption is capped at twenty percent, transparent, and completely disentangled from the public goods funding.

106
00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:29.000
Your current system can't say any of those things. The Timeline: From zero dollars to Ending Death.

107
00:11:30.060 --> 00:11:35.040
You want to end war and disease. You need one billion dollars in papers.

108
00:11:35.500 --> 00:11:40.160
You currently have zero dollars in papers (probably). Here's the recipe.

109
00:11:41.140 --> 00:11:48.000
Phase one: Proof That Voting Works (Months one to three). You build a simple version of Wishocracy.

110
00:11:48.840 --> 00:11:56.120
Basically a referendum platform where humans vote on whether to redirect one percent of the military budget to curing diseases.

111
00:11:56.640 --> 00:12:03.340
If anyone uses it, you've proven humans will participate in democracy when you make it easy and give them points.

112
00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:11.860
You show this to angel investors. Angel investors are humans who give you papers based on a PowerPoint and a dream.

113
00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:16.780
On Wishonia this is called "mental illness," but on Earth it's called "Silicon Valley."

114
00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:23.560
Phase two: Scale the Marketing, Hire Professional Bribers (Months four to eighteen).

115
00:12:24.160 --> 00:12:26.910
Humans will vote when you make it easy and reward participation.

116
00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:35.080
You've proven that. Now you raise more papers from venture capitalists (humans who gamble professionally while wearing suits).

117
00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:39.480
You use these papers to market the referendum to millions of voters.

118
00:12:39.900 --> 00:12:46.600
You also hire your first professional lobbyists. Their actual job is "convince politicians that things are good."

119
00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:51.060
Phase three: The Big Paper Sale (Months nineteen to thirty-six).

120
00:12:51.700 --> 00:13:00.440
This is the final boss level. You launch VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds to raise the full one billion dollars you need.

121
00:13:00.960 --> 00:13:08.600
You overwhelm the opposition, run a global "please don't die" advertising campaign, and get the one percent treaty signed

122
00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:12.800
by actual governments who thought weapons were the only option.

123
00:13:13.360 --> 00:13:17.530
The diplomatic phase alone is much cheaper than the full campaign.

124
00:13:17.760 --> 00:13:24.020
You raise one billion dollars for high probability. See Treaty Feasibility and Cost Analysis.

125
00:13:24.860 --> 00:13:31.340
The Legal Architecture: How to Be a Charity, a Lobbying Group, and a Hedge Fund Simultaneously.

126
00:13:32.820 --> 00:13:40.840
You need to fight on three fronts to win: moral (charity), political (lobbying), and financial (investment).

127
00:13:41.520 --> 00:13:46.400
The problem is your legal system says one organization can't do all three.

128
00:13:46.900 --> 00:13:53.000
Your legal system is adorably complicated, like a board game designed by lawyers having a nightmare.

129
00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:59.800
So you build a four-part machine: The Charity (five zero one c three): This is the "brains."

130
00:14:00.200 --> 00:14:08.360
It does research and education. Rich foundations give papers here and get to feel good about themselves (plus tax deductions,

131
00:14:08.480 --> 00:14:15.460
which are like discount coupons for virtue). The Lobbying Group (five zero one c four): This is the "sword."

132
00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:20.060
It takes the research and uses it to wage unlimited political warfare.

133
00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:24.220
That sounds scary but mostly involves lunch meetings and PowerPoints.

134
00:14:25.180 --> 00:14:33.480
The Corporation (C-Corp): This is the "engine." A for-profit entity that issues the VICTORY Incentive Alignment Bonds and

135
00:14:33.480 --> 00:14:39.360
collects the papers. Yes, you need a for-profit corporation to end death.

136
00:14:39.360 --> 00:14:45.200
Your species is hilarious. The Swiss Foundation: This is the "soul."

137
00:14:45.580 --> 00:14:51.360
The parent organization owns the corporation, ensuring profits can only fund the mission.

138
00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:56.520
You put it in Switzerland because they're good at keeping things neutral and also chocolate.

139
00:14:57.240 --> 00:15:04.120
This structure lets you legally accept papers from everyone (foundations, political donors, and Wall Street) and aim them

140
00:15:04.120 --> 00:15:11.000
all at diseases instead of each other. Phase four plus: The Expansion Phases (Years four to fifty).

141
00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:18.340
The one percent treaty is just the beginning. Like all addictions, not-dying starts with a small dose and escalates.

142
00:15:18.840 --> 00:15:22.700
The real goal is eventually redirecting *most* military spending to health.

143
00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:32.040
Why Expansion Is Built Into The System. The treaty money splits eighty-ten-ten: eighty percent to clinical trials (the point),

144
00:15:32.480 --> 00:15:39.040
ten percent to investors (the bribe), and ten percent to political incentives (the bribe for the other kind of human).

145
00:15:39.640 --> 00:15:46.800
That last slice is the interesting part, because it grows every time the treaty expands: In phase three, spanning years

146
00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:53.920
one to three, the treaty is one percent, creating a political incentive pool of two point seven two billion dollars per

147
00:15:53.920 --> 00:15:58.720
year. The treaty passes, and humans cautiously try not dying.

148
00:15:58.780 --> 00:16:05.920
In phase four, spanning years four to seven, the treaty rises to two percent, with five point four four billion dollars

149
00:16:05.920 --> 00:16:11.960
per year in the incentive pool. Politicians compete to expand (they've discovered voters like living).

150
00:16:12.700 --> 00:16:20.320
In phase five, spanning years eight to twelve, the treaty rises to five percent, with thirteen point six billion dollars

151
00:16:20.320 --> 00:16:26.360
per year in the incentive pool. The health lobby rivals the defense lobby and lobbyists switch suits.

152
00:16:27.220 --> 00:16:34.740
In phase six, spanning years thirteen to twenty, the treaty reaches ten percent, creating twenty-seven point two billion

153
00:16:34.740 --> 00:16:41.800
dollars per year in the incentive pool. "Funded pragmatic clinical trials" becomes the most rewarded phrase in politics.

154
00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:50.060
In phase seven, spanning years twenty-one to thirty-five, the treaty reaches twenty-five percent, with sixty-eight billion

155
00:16:50.060 --> 00:16:56.540
dollars per year in the incentive pool. Superpowers compete on health outcomes (much less radioactive).

156
00:16:57.160 --> 00:17:05.079
In phase eight, spanning years thirty-six to fifty, the treaty reaches fifty percent or more, with over one hundred and

157
00:17:05.079 --> 00:17:11.819
thirty-six billion dollars per year in the incentive pool. Historians write confused books about why this took so long.

158
00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:17.880
Here's Why It Keeps Growing. Bond investors get ten percent of all treaty funds.

159
00:17:18.280 --> 00:17:22.240
At one percent, that's two hundred and seventy-two percent returns.

160
00:17:22.540 --> 00:17:28.680
At two percent, it doubles. At ten percent, they're collecting ten times their original payout.

161
00:17:28.980 --> 00:17:35.220
So they will call their senator and say "please expand the treaty," not because they care about diseases but because they

162
00:17:35.220 --> 00:17:41.900
care about money. You don't have to ask them to do this. They will do it automatically, the way a plant grows toward sunlight

163
00:17:41.900 --> 00:17:45.140
except the sunlight is money and the plant is a billionaire.

164
00:17:45.720 --> 00:17:54.120
You've built a defense lobby in reverse. Politicians see their Incentive Alignment Bond, or I.A.B.-funded rewards, grow

165
00:17:54.120 --> 00:18:01.500
with each expansion. By Stage four, the political incentive pool (twenty-seven point two billion dollars per year) exceeds

166
00:18:01.500 --> 00:18:09.520
all current global lobbying combined. At that point, "I support pragmatic clinical trial funding" becomes the most profitable

167
00:18:09.520 --> 00:18:15.880
sentence a politician can say, which means they will say it constantly, which means they will eventually believe it.

168
00:18:16.400 --> 00:18:25.040
This is how your species forms convictions. The Endgame. By twenty seventy-five, the math becomes irresistible: Over one

169
00:18:25.040 --> 00:18:32.360
point three six trillion dollars flows to health annually. Over one hundred and thirty-six billion dollars funds political

170
00:18:32.360 --> 00:18:40.950
incentives (more than all lobbying ever). Over one point zero eight eight trillion dollars funds pragmatic clinical trials.

171
00:18:41.060 --> 00:18:44.900
The one percent treaty isn't the goal. It's the first one percent.

172
00:18:45.740 --> 00:18:51.400
Every investor and every politician makes more money if the number goes up, so they will push the number up.

173
00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:57.280
How far it goes depends on whether curing diseases turns out to be more popular than building bombs.

174
00:18:58.140 --> 00:19:06.350
Given that diseases kill approximately everyone and bombs kill approximately fewer people than diseases, the odds seem favorable.

175
00:19:06.600 --> 00:19:08.880
But you're humans, so nothing is certain.
